WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.035
So how far are
you coming from?

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.003
I come from South.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.904
OK.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:05.605
All the way South?

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.373
Yeah.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.107
Coming in and going to--

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:07.941
heading North.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:08.875
Heading North, yeah.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.442
OK.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.443
OK.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.544
Yeah, we are rounding
up these horses.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.379
Oh yeah.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.613
Yeah.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.118
My horses had strayed from
the swampy Sean Roundup.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.554
The one I'm riding
has a name, Buckshot.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:24.023
[music playing]

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.326
All these horses
belong to the community

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.094
where these guys are from.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:30.163
Now normally, these
horses are running wild,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.633
so they had to round them up.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.070
The horses are being taken to a
ranch a few days ride from here

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.506
to sit out the worst
of the rainy season.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.674
[music playing]

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.343
Hut.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.246
As a thank you for
finding their horses,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.582
the cowboys invite me for food.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:53.286
I join a rider called Chardo
to help him set up camp.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:56.790
Whoa.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.092
Whoa.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.493
What is that?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.662
Anaconda.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.364
Right there.

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.032
He's definitely
freaked out horses.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.902
[music playing]

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:12.372
This monster snake is
right on the trail.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:15.542
We got to get it
safely out of the way.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.976
That's a big snake.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.011
Whoa.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:18.945
Whoa.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:22.382
[music playing]

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.052
Here.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.388
You can see those.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:33.593
Just rows and rows of
really sharp teeth.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.564
Those are jaws
that mean business.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:43.169
The snake stays hidden
in murky water like this.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:48.007
You can see how that camouflage
once it's submerges itself

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.310
just a little bit
below the water,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.546
it just simply disappears.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.082
When they're active
like this one,

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.318
it usually means they're
looking for prey.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:02.422
It's waiting for anything
that can fit into the jaws

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.524
of the snake that's fair game.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:09.128
And these snakes can
easily eat an animal size

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.531
of a pig wandering
through these waters,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.434
getting a drink of
water, and boom.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.370
And it would constrict
that prey to death

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.773
so it couldn't breathe, stops
the blood flow of that animal,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.842
the animal eventually
passes out.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.012
And then the animal is safe
to eat, it'll find its head,

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.914
and then eat whatever
it caught head first.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.684
[music playing]

